{
  "summary": "User Hannah Lee (user_id 12, Finance, Payroll Specialist, active account, not blocked, zero failed logins) reports an email from 'IT Support' asking her to reply with her password to finish account setup. She did NOT reply or disclose anything. Checked: account is active and not locked; quarantine for her mailbox is empty, so the message was not caught by spam filtering. Account shows must_change_password=true and password last set 2026-10-11, which may be relevant to the 'account setup' lure. Sender address and exact subject are not in the ticket (subject given as 'email from IT?'), so the sender still needs to be pulled from her mailbox for review. Per KB-008 this must be reviewed by security so the sender can be blocked for everyone if needed. Needed: review the message, block the sender, and check whether other users received it. No password reset or sign-in block is needed unless the user later reports a click or entry (KB-029).",
  "reason": "Suspected phishing reported by user; KB-008 requires escalation so security can review and block the sender"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for reporting this, and you did the right thing by not replying. IT Support will never ask for your password by email, so treat that message as a scam. Please don't click any links, reply to it, or forward it to colleagues. Leave it in your mailbox for now so our security team can examine it. We've passed it to them and they'll look into the sender and block it if needed. If you clicked a link or entered your password anywhere, let us know right away.",
  "internal_note": "Escalated per KB-008 (always escalate reported suspicious email). Checked: user_id 12, Hannah Lee, Finance, Payroll Specialist. Account active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, must_change_password=true, password last set 2026-10-11. Quarantine for her mailbox is empty, so the message was not caught by filtering. The user did not reply or disclose credentials, so no password reset, unlock, or sign-in block was done. Sender address and exact subject are missing from the ticket and need pulling from her mailbox. Security should block the sender and check for other recipients. The triage marked possible_social_engineering=false, but the email is a credential-harvesting lure, so this was not downgraded. Escalation id 1.",
